<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech parliament begins final debate on '97 budget.</title>
<headline>Czech parliament begins final debate on '97 budget.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lower house of Czech parliament has begun debate on the third and final reading of the government's draft 1997 budget, with a final vote expected later on Friday.</p>
<p>After an agreement of the three coalition parties to support the budget on Thursday, the minority government needs two opposition votes to assure approval of the planned balanced budget of 549.1 billion crowns, up from 491 billion in 1996.</p>
</text>
